1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,750
Oh, dear.

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,460
Penny, have you been recording shows

3
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:09,580
- on our DVR again? - No.

4
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:12,500
Answer honestly. This is not a trial.

5
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:15,380
That'll come later.

6
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,140
Absolutely not.

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,010
Help me out here. I can't afford another demerit.

8
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:21,270
Yeah.

9
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,580
Uh... maybe we were hacked.

10
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:26,550
You know, the Chinese have been hacking everything lately.

11
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:32,520
Why would the Chinese make our DVR record Paul Blart: Mall Cop?

12
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,100
I don't know.

13
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:38,370
It's a fat guy on a Segway. That's funny everywhere.

14
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:40,170
I'm deleting it.

15
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,460
Well, hang on.

16
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,460
Maybe the Chinese haven't finished watching it yet.

17
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,520
You know, if you're trying to make space on the DVR,

18
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:49,360
why don't you just get rid of

19
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,840
some of the stuff you've already watched?

20
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,760
Like, um... Alphas.

21
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,530
No, that's the season two finale.

22
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,740
That was quite the cliffhanger.

23
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,010
I'm going to re-watch it before season three starts.

24
00:00:58,010 --> 00:01:00,860
There is no season three. They canceled that show.

25
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:05,440
Well, they can't cancel it.

26
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,650
It ended on a cliffhanger.

27
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,470
- They did. - Uh, Sheldon,

28
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,200
there are two dumplings left. Do you want them?

29
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:11,970
Dumplings?

30
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:14,530
Don't you understand what's going on here?

31
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,530
As a rule, no.

32
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:19,670
That show ended with all the residents of New York

33
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:21,420
either dead or unconscious.

34
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:23,340
Now I'll never know what happened.

35
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,490
Well, why don't you make up your own ending?

36
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:28,860
Oh, sure, what a wonderful idea.

37
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:29,360
And after that,

38
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,490
I'll make up my own rules of oral hygiene.

39
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:34,890
You know, instead of flossing, I'll rub pudding on my gums.

40
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:36,660
I'm going to get the number of the SyFy Channel

41
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:37,770
and give them what for.

42
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:39,420
Oh, please, don't do that.

43
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,930
No. They can't just cancel a show like Alphas.

44
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,770
You know? They have to help the viewers let go.

45
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:47,120
Firefly did a movie to wrap things up.

46
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:50,220
Buffy the Vampire Slayer continued on as a comic book.

47
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:53,540
Heroes gradually lowered the quality season by season

48
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:56,350
till we were grateful it ended.

49
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:58,950
I feel bad for whoever gets that phone call.

50
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:00,040
Ah, don't.

51
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,980
If they didn't want to be yelled at by crazy nerds,

52
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:04,290
they shouldn't have started a Sci-Fi channel.

53
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,610
I think you're gonna be really happy

54
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,880
with this security camera.

55
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:34,990
The optics are great,

56
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,830
it's got infrared technology,

57
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:40,230
and there's even a backup battery when the power goes out.

58
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:40,800
Whatever.

59
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,070
I can see my little princess

60
00:02:42,070 --> 00:02:43,790
while I'm at work, right?

61
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:48,260
Why can't you just watch porn like a regular guy?

62
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,930
I need your laptop so I can configure the software.

63
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:54,480
Wait, hold on.

64
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:56,000
This is weird.

65
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,690
What?

66
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:58,480
I was Googling that girl I've been dating,

67
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,670
and I found her blog.

68
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:00,810
Cool.

69
00:03:00,810 --> 00:03:02,010
Anything juicy?

70
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:05,970
She said she recently went on a date with a guy named Roger?

71
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,030
And he's Indian?

72
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:12,630
And he's an astrophysicist, too?

73
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,990
You know what's going on, don't you?

74
00:03:16,990 --> 00:03:18,180
Yes. Mummy was right.

75
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:21,460
American girls are sexually voracious devils.

76
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,900
I can't believe I have to explain this.

77
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:27,380
People change names on blogs to protect their privacy.

78
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:30,280
Roger is Raj.

79
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:33,090
I always thought, if I had a white name,

80
00:03:33,090 --> 00:03:34,810
it would be Gavin.

81
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:38,900
Keep reading. What does it say?

82
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,620
No, no, I don't know if I should.

83
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:43,030
If she wanted me to know about her blog, she would've told me.

84
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:44,750
It's almost like I'm reading her diary.

85
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:47,500
That's exactly what it's like. Keep reading.

86
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,510
No, this is creepy.

87
00:03:49,510 --> 00:03:51,970
Oh, I think we were looking at creepy in the rearview mirror

88
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:53,770
when I put up that camera.

89
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:58,910
It's not creepy. Don't listen to him.

90
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:03,570
Oh, look who's got the sweetest kisses.

91
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:13,080
Should I go?

92
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,110
With all the TV Sheldon was talking about,

93
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,870
I had the greatest idea ever.

94
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,990
It even blows away my idea

95
00:04:22,990 --> 00:04:26,370
for a Star Wars themed coffee shop called "Brewbacca's."

96
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:30,740
You need to watch Buffy the Vampire Slayer.

97
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,560
It is the perfect show for the two of us.

98
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,030
It's got action and jokes

99
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,840
and hot vampires and romance. I cannot oversell this!

100
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:38,240
What do you say?

101
00:04:38,810 --> 00:04:40,860
It's 6:30 in the morning.

102
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:45,520
I thought you grew up on a farm.

103
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:50,640
Hello, SyFy Network?

104
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:53,940
Yeah, this is your vice president of programming.

105
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:57,670
Now, we have made a horrible mistake regarding Alphas.

106
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,500
Yeah, we need to uncancel it immediately.

107
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,920
Well, you just put me through to the people who handle that,

108
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,050
you tell them it's me,

109
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:05,860
and I don't want to answer a lot of questions

110
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:08,890
about if I really am who I say I am, you know?

111
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,880
I just... I want this done.

112
00:05:11,610 --> 00:05:14,460
No, I am not the person who just called.

113
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:18,180
That man was clearly a cowboy.

114
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,330
Yeah, who was plumb concerned

115
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:22,570
about y'all canceling his favorite show.

116
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:26,670
Why do they keep hanging up on me?

117
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,190
I'm sorry you're upset.

118
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,770
You know, Sheldon, sometimes people seek the comfort

119
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:34,770
of physical contact in moments like this.

120
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:40,840
I am not flying back to Texas

121
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,370
just so my mom can give me a hug.

122
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:46,290
Okay.

123
00:05:46,290 --> 00:05:48,190
Well, what I think is going on here

124
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:51,020
is you have a pathological need for closure.

125
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:53,160
Oh, that's nonsense.

126
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:56,140
I mean, you tell me stories about your day all the time.

127
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:58,140
I don't care how they end.

128
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:02,250
You know, I might be able to help you with this.

129
00:06:02,250 --> 00:06:04,390
There's a whole field of behavioral neuroscience

130
00:06:04,390 --> 00:06:07,180
that examines ways to retrain your neural pathways

131
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:09,240
so stuff like this bothers you less.

132
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,230
Yeah, but I just told you,

133
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:12,680
I don't have a problem with closure.

134
00:06:12,710 --> 00:06:13,830
You sure about that?

135
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,530
Oh, quite sure.

136
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,090
That proves nothing.

137
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,900
Ready to go to lunch?

138
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,710
Do you think I'm feminine?

139
00:06:36,290 --> 00:06:37,830
Yeah. Let's go.

140
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:39,930
Thanks a lot.

141
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,440
What's going on?

142
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:43,990
I broke down, and I read Lucy's blog.

143
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:45,300
And in one of the entries,

144
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,510
she said, when we first met,

145
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:48,850
I struck her as a little feminine.

146
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,400
Just a little? That's great.

147
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,870
I have to talk to her about this.

148
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,610
Oh, geez, why do you girls always want to talk about things?

149
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,000
Listen to me,

150
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,590
if she's writing about your relationship,

151
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:02,320
use it to your advantage.

152
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,060
Rig the game.

153
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:05,470
Well, that doesn't seem fair.

154
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,900
Is it fair that girls like confident, normal guys

155
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:10,280
more than nervous weirdos?

156
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:11,440
No, it's not.

157
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,690
I've always thought that was unfair.

158
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:18,320
So take what's in that blog and use it to get her pants off.

159
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,290
Why do you have to make everything so filthy?

160
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:22,190
Why couldn't you just say the blog is like

161
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,760
her giving me the key to her heart?

162
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,670
"The key to her heart."

163
00:07:26,690 --> 00:07:27,790
That's nice.

164
00:07:27,790 --> 00:07:28,850
Were you quoting someone

165
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:31,290
or is it tattooed on the small of your back?

166
00:07:31,970 --> 00:07:35,670
I was quoting a man who knows a thing or two about women:

167
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:37,880
Sir Elton John.

168
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:47,880
So, did you love it?

169
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,130
Of course you loved it. How could you not love it?

170
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:51,020
Tell me how much you loved it.

171
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,780
It was cute.

172
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,310
Oh, don't say cute.

173
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,460
That's the worst.

174
00:07:58,460 --> 00:07:59,410
What's wrong with cute?

175
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,630
It just makes things seem small.

176
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:03,310
It diminishes them.

177
00:08:03,310 --> 00:08:06,370
So you want me to stop calling your little tushy cute?

178
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:09,670
You can try, but nobody's gonna believe you.

179
00:08:11,790 --> 00:08:14,390
I just... I don't understand how you can watch a show that great

180
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,990
and not be excited by it.

181
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:17,430
I liked it. I'm excited.

182
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:19,940
Well, then, tell your face.

183
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,540
What do you want from me?

184
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:23,660
You know what?

185
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,830
Never mind. We gave it a shot.

186
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:26,280
Let's just see what else is on.

187
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,940
Oh, come on, don't be like that.

188
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,570
I'm sorry I called it cute.

189
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:32,360
- Let's watch another one. - Really?

190
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,500
Yeah, it was fun.

191
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,480
Kind of reminded me of my high school.

192
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,760
But instead of vampires, we had meth heads.

193
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:42,940
But both came out at night and had messed up teeth.

194
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,750
All right, cool.

195
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:46,370
I-I think you'll like the next one better.

196
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:48,950
All the cheerleaders are suffering from an evil curse.

197
00:08:48,950 --> 00:08:51,320
Oh. Well, that's like my high school, too.

198
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:54,480
But instead of a curse, it was crabs.

199
00:08:57,610 --> 00:08:59,530
I've come up with a series of exercises

200
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:02,310
to help with your compulsive need for closure.

201
00:09:02,310 --> 00:09:05,450
I take issue with the word "compulsive."

202
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:07,640
All I'm saying is,

203
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:11,700
we live in a world where closure isn't always an op...

204
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:24,860
...Tion. Okay.

205
00:09:26,430 --> 00:09:29,300
For the sake of argument, let's say I have a problem.

206
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:31,670
What would be your plan for addressing it?

207
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:33,980
I'm going to recondition your brain

208
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:38,690
so that the need for completion isn't so overwhelming.

209
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:42,360
By playing tic-tac-toe?

210
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,660
Yep. Your turn.

211
00:09:43,660 --> 00:09:45,530
Oh, Amy.

212
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,820
And you wonder why people think neuroscience

213
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:50,670
is nothing but a goofy game for diaper babies.

214
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:55,170
Tic-tac-toe can only end in win, lose or draw...

215
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:57,910
none of which will deny me closure.

216
00:09:58,010 --> 00:10:00,960
Especially since I'm about to win.

217
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:13,430
B-But we didn't finish.

218
00:10:13,430 --> 00:10:14,420
Exactly.

219
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,720
How does that make you feel?

220
00:10:18,190 --> 00:10:20,370
The same way any normal person would.

221
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:22,460
Feel like I want to peel off my own face

222
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:24,300
and tear it in two and then again and again

223
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,870
until I have a handful of Sheldon-face confetti.

224
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,800
And that's exactly the feeling we want to address

225
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:30,790
with this course of treatment.

226
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:32,810
Yeah, or you could pitch in, grab a nostril

227
00:10:32,810 --> 00:10:34,680
and help me get this face off.

228
00:10:35,310 --> 00:10:37,030
Come on, you can do this.

229
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:39,680
You don't know what it's like to feel completely frustrated.

230
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,290
To have a-a desire build up within you

231
00:10:42,290 --> 00:10:45,610
and be denied any opportunity for release.

232
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:55,270
Yeah, sounds like a drag.

233
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:09,890
Okay, help me out here.

234
00:11:09,890 --> 00:11:12,190
Why does he love this show so much?

235
00:11:12,190 --> 00:11:15,080
Well, there was action, it was funny.

236
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:18,710
I mean, you do get that usually the monster chases the pretty girl,

237
00:11:18,710 --> 00:11:21,750
but this time the pretty girl chases the monsters?

238
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:25,680
Yippee, it's backwards. I get it.

239
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:29,510
Why does this bother you so much?

240
00:11:29,510 --> 00:11:30,990
I don't know.

241
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,350
It's just, he's so passionate about so many different things.

242
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:34,790
I just don't get that way.

243
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:36,140
Do you?

244
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:39,030
Well, sure. I'm pretty passionate about science.

245
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,140
I remember the first time I looked through a microscope

246
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:43,620
and saw millions of tiny microorganisms.

247
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,850
It was like a whole other universe.

248
00:11:45,850 --> 00:11:50,220
If I wanted to, I could wipe it out with my thumb like a god.

249
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,480
See? I wish I had some of that fire in my life.

250
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,270
I mean, I want to care about things

251
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:58,030
and get excited like you guys.

252
00:11:58,030 --> 00:11:59,680
Well, there's no reason you can't.

253
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:00,510
You think?

254
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,680
Absolutely. All we need to do is spend

255
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,940
a little time and find something you're passionate about.

256
00:12:06,430 --> 00:12:08,670
That sounds like a lot of work.

257
00:12:13,090 --> 00:12:14,560
Hey, what's up?

258
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:17,050
Uh, Lucy's coming over. I need some advice.

259
00:12:17,050 --> 00:12:21,050
However long you think the foreplay should be, triple it.

260
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:26,390
Just tell me which one you think is more manly.

261
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:28,850
This hockey jersey or...

262
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:31,120
this football jersey.

263
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,990
I don't know. Go with hockey.

264
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:36,660
Good-- black is more slimming.

265
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,610
Oh, that's her.

266
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:42,380
I got to go be butch. Toodles.

267
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:49,620
Come in.

268
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:53,260
Oh, look how cute your little doggy is.

269
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:54,900
Yeah, well, I wouldn't get too close.

270
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,230
If I give the right command in German,

271
00:12:56,230 --> 00:12:58,160
she'll rip your face off.

272
00:13:02,690 --> 00:13:07,200
* O'er the land of the free *

273
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:12,290
* And the home of the... *

274
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:13,720
Next.

275
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,690
That's quite an impressive layout, isn't it?

276
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,960
Yes.

277
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:29,060
Let's box it up.

278
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,960
"Let's box it up."

279
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:43,200
That's enough.

280
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:47,130
Sheldon, Sheldon, give it!

281
00:13:49,590 --> 00:13:53,230
Okay, Sheldon, make a wish and blow out the candles.

282
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,650
Oops, missed one.

283
00:14:00,650 --> 00:14:02,700
Now your wish can't come true.

284
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:07,530
Lucky for you, 'cause I wished you were dead.

285
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:13,230
I like your jersey.

286
00:14:13,230 --> 00:14:15,220
Thanks. I love hockey.

287
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:16,820
Oh, cool. So does my dad.

288
00:14:16,820 --> 00:14:18,850
We watched it all the time growing up.

289
00:14:18,850 --> 00:14:20,790
Who's your favorite player?

290
00:14:25,130 --> 00:14:28,510
Not Brian Boitano, that's for sure.

291
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:31,800
How's your burrito?

292
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,880
It's still a little frozen in the middle.

293
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,770
Probably because I didn't read the instructions.

294
00:14:35,770 --> 00:14:38,400
No wrapper's going to tell me what to do.

295
00:14:38,890 --> 00:14:41,300
Unless his name is Jay-Z.

296
00:14:42,290 --> 00:14:43,910
Is something going on?

297
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:44,880
What do you mean?

298
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,670
Well, you're acting all weird.

299
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:47,350
And I'm pretty weird,

300
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:49,930
so I think I know what I'm talking about.

301
00:14:50,930 --> 00:14:54,350
I don't know. Maybe it's all those steroids I've been taking.

302
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:56,940
I think I'm gonna go.

303
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,620
Thank you for the burrito and the pork rinds

304
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:00,630
and the 20-minute lecture

305
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:03,790
on why monster trucks are better than regular trucks.

306
00:15:04,730 --> 00:15:06,510
Wait, wait.

307
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:11,160
I-I found your blog where you wrote about me.

308
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,730
Oh. I kind of just write that for myself.

309
00:15:13,730 --> 00:15:15,390
I didn't think anybody actually read it.

310
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:17,210
No kidding. You didn't make it easy to find.

311
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:19,800
I spent hours digging around online.

312
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:23,030
For the record, you have excellent credit scores.

313
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:24,560
And your diabetic aunt seems

314
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,080
to be adjusting to her new leg just fine.

315
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:32,290
Why were you acting so strange tonight?

316
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:34,110
You called me feminine.

317
00:15:34,110 --> 00:15:35,250
And I...

318
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,850
I wanted you to think I was more manly.

319
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:40,610
Raj, I didn't say "feminine" was a bad thing.

320
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:42,810
I meant that you're sweet and thoughtful

321
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:44,350
and your skin looks so much like caramel,

322
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:46,970
I just want to dip an apple in your face.

323
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,640
I do have a pretty balls-to-the-wall

324
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:51,730
moisturizing regimen.

325
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,060
So, are you okay?

326
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:56,280
Yeah.

327
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,610
Good.

328
00:15:58,070 --> 00:15:59,670
Do you even like hockey?

329
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:01,020
No.

330
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:02,330
Bought this at the Staples Center

331
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:04,460
when I went to see Taylor Swift.

332
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:10,280
So, I was thinking how excited you get

333
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,870
about stuff like Buffy or science

334
00:16:12,870 --> 00:16:15,290
or which TV remote you and Sheldon should buy.

335
00:16:15,290 --> 00:16:16,860
The "Harmony One" was fine.

336
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:18,410
We didn't need to upgrade to the 1100,

337
00:16:18,410 --> 00:16:21,440
which he knows is too big for my hand.

338
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:25,630
See, that's the kind of passion I didn't think I had.

339
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:28,870
But then I realized I'm passionate about you.

340
00:16:28,970 --> 00:16:32,730
Oh... my cute little tushy strikes again.

341
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,050
No, I'm serious.

342
00:16:36,050 --> 00:16:37,770
Look, I've always had these plans.

343
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:40,430
I was gonna be in movies and live this glamorous life,

344
00:16:40,430 --> 00:16:41,580
and anything less than that

345
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:43,680
just wasn't worth getting excited about.

346
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,380
Those things can still happen.

347
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:46,700
Oh, obviously it's gonna happen.

348
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:49,620
Yeah, a psychic at a bachelorette party told me so.

349
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:52,040
Anyway, what I meant was...

350
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:54,310
I shouldn't wait, you know?

351
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:57,870
I've got you, I've got Sheldon,

352
00:16:57,870 --> 00:16:59,910
all these wonderful friends.

353
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:02,270
My life is exciting right now.

354
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:04,740
That's a big deal.

355
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:07,120
It is, isn't it?

356
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:11,190
So, does that mean we get to do stuff

357
00:17:11,190 --> 00:17:13,650
like talk about cool shows or get dressed up

358
00:17:13,650 --> 00:17:16,770
in matching costumes and go to Comic-Con?

359
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:21,300
Leonard, I had an epiphany, not a stroke.

360
00:17:25,190 --> 00:17:28,450
Amy, I must say, I was skeptical at first,

361
00:17:28,450 --> 00:17:31,510
but this has truly been a transformative evening.

362
00:17:31,510 --> 00:17:34,170
I'm a little surprised to hear you feeling so positive.

363
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,720
Well, you're an excellent neuroscientist,

364
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:40,150
you're a wonderful girlfriend, and...

365
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,750
And?

366
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:47,070
Doesn't matter, does it?

367
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:50,500
I'm proud of you, Sheldon.

368
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:55,840
And a complete sucker.

369
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:01,790
Oh, yeah.

370
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:12,130
There he is.

371
00:18:14,830 --> 00:18:21,030
* And the home of the brave... *

372
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,180
Don't stop. Yes, keep going.

373
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:29,450
Just like that. Almost there, almost there.

374
00:18:35,050 --> 00:18:36,370
Sheldon, you big weirdo,

375
00:18:36,370 --> 00:18:38,480
I want you to know that I love that you're in my life.

376
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,890
I love you, too.

377
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:52,650
Hello. Uh, is this the Bruce Miller who wrote

378
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:54,990
the season finale of Alphas?

379
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:58,980
Oh, smashing. Yeah, you already sound nicer

380
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,790
than the last Bruce Miller who suggested

381
00:19:00,790 --> 00:19:03,510
I have sexual relations with myself.

382
00:19:03,730 --> 00:19:04,900
Yeah, now, down to business.

383
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,080
Um, your show ended on a cliffhanger.

384
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:10,390
Could you please tell me how you planned to resolve it?

385
00:19:14,510 --> 00:19:16,090
I see.

386
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:17,730
Well, that all stinks.

387
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:20,140
No wonder you got canceled. Bye.

